{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one","id":1554346,"title":"As a HtV player - is getting bit by a WtF Werewolf part of becoming one?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-13T12:38:51-07:00","id":1554346,"title":"As a HtV player - is getting bit by a WtF Werewolf part of becoming one?","content":"Just curious! My GM will have his own answer, but I like thinking about these things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T12:55:57-07:00","id":1554347,"title":"","content":"No (Mostly).<br /> <br /> A bite can sometimes cause a person to become one of the wolf-blooded, but it's not common or entirely clear why it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-13T13:39:03-07:00","id":1554348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one#post1554346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious! My GM will have his own answer, but I like thinking about these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>From 1e Core forward, Forsaken has put forth the explanation for the &quot;werewolf bites make people into werewolves&quot; myth as it pertains to the Uratha as the combination of a) the First Change being something that spirits and werewolves can at least kind of see coming and b) werewolves being able to track creatures whose blood they have tasted.<br /> <br /> Essentially, when those stories are describing the werewolves that Forsaken is about rather than a superficially similar type of monster, you turn into a werewolf after getting bitten by a werewolf because you were getting close to becoming a werewolf and that werewolf could tell and wanted to keep tabs on you for when you first turn into a werewolf (an event that often involves you flipping out and killing shit in a way that will need to be managed by a werewolf pack even if they don't go on to recruit or kill you).<br /> <br /> Ironically, getting bitten by a werewolf usually makes a mortal <i>less</i> likely to spontaneously become Wolf-Blooded, as that requires a dramatic failure on the roll to resist Lunacy and inflicting lethal damage (such as from a bite or claws) gives the victims of a werewolf's Lunacy a bonus to that roll \u2014 if anything, especially in cases where the victim was severely wounded, a werewolf bite is more likely to serve as the basis for taking up the Vigil, as exceptional success refills their Willpower and allows them to recall the events they witnessed in perfect clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T16:31:50-07:00","id":1554436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one?p=1554347#post1554347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No (Mostly).<br /> <br /> A bite can sometimes cause a person to become one of the wolf-blooded, but it's not common or entirely clear why it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolf-blooded being vaguely akin to Kinfolk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T17:46:50-07:00","id":1554438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one?p=1554436#post1554436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf-blooded being vaguely akin to Kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but more Werewolf support characters than breeding stock.<br /> <br /> To expand on Michael's post, werewolves can Inflict Lunacy, a supernaturally-tinged fear of werewolves. It affects people who see werewolves up close, forcing a Breaking Point roll. With successes they sort of re-invent their memory of what happened to make a safer fit with their view of the world. But a Dramatic Failure on the roll means the character becomes Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Some of the Wolf-Blooded Tells (abilities with bonuses and disadvantages) lean into traditional takes on werewolves. With the Anger Issues Tell, for instance, they have a trigger for rage and can turn into the near-human form, gaining some Strength and regeneration while it happens. They aren't a werewolf but someone seeing it happen and jumping to that conclusion would probably be justified in thinking they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T18:53:40-07:00","id":1554439,"title":"","content":"There's also, weirdly enough, a Wolf Gift Facet that fits the myth: any Uratha with at least Purity 1 and an Experience to spend can gain the ability to reflexively spend 1 Essence on a successful damaging bite to a living non-Uratha target to inflict the Moon Taint Condition, which applies the Poisoned Tilt for its duration (inflicting damage in action scenes unless the victim succeeds at a Stamina + Resolve roll each turn) and making it so that the first time they see the full moon while the Condition applies they have to succeed at an extended Resolve + Composure roll or else they immediately assume Dalu (near-human) form and gain the same regenerative abilities as a Primal Urge 1 werewolf while entering a Soft Rage, returning to normal when the sun rises; the only other way to clear the Condition is to poison yourself with wolfsbane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-17T20:52:03-07:00","id":1554441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one?p=1554436#post1554436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wolf-blooded being vaguely akin to Kinfolk?</div> </div> </div> </div>They may fill similar roles, but not all, and there are things they do that Kinfolk don't.<br /> <br /> Wolf-Blooded are less family and more &quot;infection&quot;, although the most common &quot;vector&quot; is still family lines. There are a bunch of ways to become Wolf-Blooded, but what they gave above is the only one with actual rules attached. Even then, it's not considered in lore the most common source, or actually common at all.<br /> <br /> A Wolf-Blooded is a human (not a wolf, never) intrinsically changed by contact with the spiritual nature of Father Wolf, usually through contact with Uratha or other Wolf-Blooded. <u><b>They</b></u> are the werewolves of legend more often than not, and develop powers. A person bitten by a Werewolf, either true Uratha or Wolf-Blooded, <b><u>may</u></b> become a Wolf-Blooded, and it isn't hard for a &quot;werewolf outbreak&quot; plot to be built around that.<br /> <br /> Uratha work within societies called &quot;Packs&quot;. They're a combination of WtA Packs, Septs and Kinfolk cults. Some packs are small and limited to a couple werewolves, but they can be huge groups and include people of all kinds and templates, including no template at all, be them humans, spirits or animals. In practice most of the roles Kinfolk filled in WtA are now filled by perfectly normal humans that work for them. There are powers and effects to manage and empower the Pack, so those people are sufficiently protected against werewolf shenanigans for this to work.<br /> <br /> Overall and following CoD's method, things are far more flexible and nuanced. A lot of things may fill a lot of roles, including the very role of Werewolf. The bite thing is false in its most basic assumption, but there are a lot of possible powers, creatures and edge cases that may make it actually work under certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Do not get bitten by a Uratha. If you do, take some wolfsbane, just remembers that it's extremely poisonous and possibly fatal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T20:49:00-08:00","id":1557697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one#post1554346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious! My GM will have his own answer, but I like thinking about these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is not. But there is a correlation that might have bene the origin of such a myth.<br /> <br /> The opening story for Forsaken 1E reveals that they are performing a ritual that will allow them to track a future werewolf who is about to undergo the First Change. But in order to complete the ritual, they need to bite him first.<br /> <br /> Hence, they find the future recruit and give him a nip, before adding his blood to the ritual ingredients. After that, they're able to keep tabs on him, and approach later when he's about to wolf out in the street.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T21:48:28-08:00","id":1557701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1554346-as-a-htv-player-is-getting-bit-by-a-wtf-werewolf-part-of-becoming-one?p=1557697#post1557697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The opening story for Forsaken 1E reveals that they are performing a ritual that will allow them to track a future werewolf who is about to undergo the First Change. But in order to complete the ritual, they need to bite him first.<br /> <br /> Hence, they find the future recruit and give him a nip, before adding his blood to the ritual ingredients. After that, they're able to keep tabs on him, and approach later when he's about to wolf out in the street.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Shared Scent ritual, which allows a werewolf who has recently tasted a target's blood to share that taste with other werewolves for the purposes of the normal ability of werewolves to track that prey, mentioned earlier in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-21T12:41:41-08:00","id":1557812,"title":"","content":"The cavet on what everyone else has (correctly) said being that weird shit happens all the time in Chronicles of Darkness. If you want to have werewolves who spread their curse via bites, it can still happen and would probably freak the Forsaken right out. It could be they aren't Forsaken, but a Deviant with the Transmissible Form whose curse makes them a better fit for the pop culture werewolf. It could be they <i><b>are </b></i>Forsaken and something is altering their spiritual makeup (Ivory Claw experiments? Geryo? The Contagion? An <i>indigim</i>? Take your pick) so they to become infectious. Maybe they are Claimed by a wolf-spirit whose bite makes victims vulberable to similar spirits? Or perhaps they are simply a one-off horror without connection to the rest of the Chronicles of Darkness that acts as a foil for the Pack. If it makes a good story, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}